          "text": "She has known severe COPD (FEV1 30% predicted, home O2, previous ITU avoided by choice). On admission she was in type 2 respiratory failure (temperature 37.8, RR 28, sats 84% on home O2, pH 7.30, PaCO2 8.1). She was treated with controlled oxygen, non-invasive ventilation (NIV), nebulisers, IV hydrocortisone transitioning to oral prednisolone, and IV then oral amoxicillin (per local guidelines). She was successfully weaned off NIV by day 3, with sats 88–90% on her home O2 at baseline. Inhaler technique was reviewed, a rescue pack was supplied, and smoking cessation was discussed (she is an ex-smoker).",
