        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with:\n- shortness of breath getting worse over 4 days\n- green sputum\n- wheeze\n\nThe team found you had an acute flare-up of your COPD. This caused a problem with your breathing called type 2 respiratory failure."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "Tests on arrival showed your oxygen levels were low and your breathing was under strain.\n\nTo treat you, the team gave you:\n- controlled oxygen\n- a breathing support machine (non-invasive ventilation, or NIV); you were weaned off this by day 3\n- nebulisers\n- a steroid (hydrocortisone) through a drip, then steroid tablets (prednisolone)\n- an antibiotic (amoxicillin) through a drip, then antibiotic tablets\n\nThe team also checked your inhaler technique and gave you a rescue pack to take home. Smoking cessation was discussed with you."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "The following have been arranged:\n- A respiratory clinic appointment in 6 weeks\n- A referral to the community respiratory team\n- Your GP will review you after this flare-up"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
